## Next work and unchanged boundary

Next is the native adapter and guardian integration: authenticate target Linux
headers/ABI, transfer exactly one listener during trusted bootstrap, install and
read back both filters, then connect kernel ID-validation/response operations to
this core before payload release. Every terminal error must retire the owned
workload. Parent-loss and deadline protection must remain independently armed:
poll readiness alone cannot prove notification receive stays nonblocking after
cancellation. Existing `RLIMIT_CORE=0` and authority/mapping exclusions must be
preserved, alongside separate setup/scratch/report/metadata/capacity bounds.

The dispatcher output boundary and lifecycle limitation from v0.108 also remain.
After integrated source closure, bounded Linux qualification and the existing
host/input/resource/real-import admission are still required. These are the
remaining parts of the existing work, not additional roadmap gates.

The S3-backed pretrained checkpoint remains the intended base; no current S3
availability check was made. Training and production stay disabled. GPU is not
needed for the next local implementation work.
